Applied the repair in src/dotenv/parser.py only: changed `_rest_of_line` from `r"[^
]*(?:|
|
)?"` to `r"[^
]*(?:
|
|)?"`.

Because the alternation now tries `
` first, error recovery consumes a CRLF as one complete newline. For an invalid first line followed by GOOD=ok, the invalid binding's original.string now includes the whole CRLF, and the valid binding starts at line 2 with original.string exactly "GOOD=ok
". LF and lone-CR handling are unchanged (they still match their single-character alternatives), and repeated invalid lines continue to be consumed one per binding. No tests, docs, other modules, or dependencies were touched.
